Assembler Version 13
====================
Assembled by: version 12 (both instgen and asm)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 12, plus expression evaluation, .data directive,
expression-aware forward reference propagation, and error module extraction:

Syntax:
- Standard 6502 mnemonic syntax (LDA, STA, etc.)
- All addressing modes (immediate, zero page, absolute, indexed, indirect)
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Character literals: 'x', '\n', '\\', '\'' (in expressions and immediate mode)
- Quoted strings in DATA with escape sequences
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment (label = value)
- Local labels with . prefix (.label), scoped to most recent global label
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators (applied to entire expression result)
- Expression evaluation with + and - operators (left-to-right, no precedence)
- Mixed expressions: hex, labels, and character literals (e.g., '9'-'0'+$01)
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly with forward reference tracking (from version 12)
- Automatic zero page vs absolute addressing based on value

Directives:
- .include filename - includes contents of another file
- .zeropage - switch to zero page section
- .code - switch to code section
- .data - declare raw byte data (new)

Error handling: same as version 12 (errors $01-$12, $13, $16), plus:
- err_invalid_operand ($14): invalid operand in expression
- err_unexpected_text ($15): unexpected text after operand

New in this version (relative to version 12):
- Expression evaluation with + and - operators
  - parse_term: parses a single value ($hex, 'char', label)
  - parse_expression: chains terms with + and - operators
  - parse_value: handles < > byte selectors then calls parse_expression
  - Left-to-right evaluation, no operator precedence
  - Character literals supported as expression terms
  - Forward references propagate through expressions (if any term is forward
    ref, entire expression is treated as forward ref via EXPR_FWDREF)
- Extended forward reference tracking for expressions
  - Version 12 introduced basic forward ref tracking for single label operands;
    this version extends IS_FWDREF propagation to multi-term expressions
  - EXPR_FWDREF accumulates forward reference status across expression terms
- .data directive: new directive form for raw byte data
- errors.asm module: error messages and interrupt handler extracted from
  main source into separate include file
- OPERAND_L/OPERAND_H aliased to HEX2/HEX1 (shared storage)
- EXPR_ACCU_L/EXPR_ACCU_H zero page variables for expression accumulator
- EXPR_FWDREF for accumulated forward reference flag in expressions
- EXPR_CARRY for saved carry from first term
- + and - added as token terminators in compare_end_of_token

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
- Standard 6502 mnemonic syntax
- All addressing modes including indirect indexed
- DATA pseudo-instruction for byte/string data
- Hex constants ($xx and $xxxx)
- Character literals in immediate mode (#'x', #'\n', etc.)
- Quoted strings with escape sequences
- Labels and label assignments
- Local labels with . prefix
- PC setting (* = $2000 and * = $FFFC)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Comments (;)
- BRK with inline error code and message (via DATA on next line)
- .include directive (environment.asm, common.asm, file_stack.asm,
  errors.asm, fwdref.asm)
- .zeropage and .code directives

New syntax used in source (relative to version 12):
- None (source uses DATA pseudo-instruction, not the new .data directive,
  because it is assembled by version 12 which does not support .data)

Note: the source does NOT use expression evaluation (no + or - operators
in operands). Expressions are a feature this assembler SUPPORTS for programs
it assembles. Version 14 is the first version whose source uses expressions,
since it is assembled by version 13.

Other source changes:
- errors.asm module extracted (error messages, interrupt handler, show_message,
  show_decimal, to_decimal include)
- fwdref.asm module for forward reference list management
- OPERAND_L/OPERAND_H aliased to HEX2/HEX1 via = assignment
- Expression accumulator variables (EXPR_ACCU_L/H, EXPR_FWDREF, EXPR_CARRY)
